{"content":[{"c":["BITHIAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Mered’s wife. Bithiah may have been a princess, or the phrase “daughter of Pharaoh” (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},") may merely indicate that she was Egyptian (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.17-18","r":"1Chr.4.17-18","rawR":"1Chr.4.17-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.17-18","value":"1Chr.4.17-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:17-18"},"). Her name (meaning “daughter of Yah”) seems to indicate that she was a Jewish convert."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Bithiah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 4:17-18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.4.17-18","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.4.17-18","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.4.17-18"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"691bde1a8203b6cec919f35fe4e8c6eb3eaa142d97a47f6cb6e352170d80bf2c","sourceItemName":"Bithiah","sourceItemOrder":331,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Bithiah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Bithiah","title":"Bithiah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}